            "y": 1
          },
          "id": 2,
          "options": {
            "content": "**Purpose.** One dashboard for every service. Pick a service in the **Service** dropdown. It replaces eight near-identical copies, which would drift apart.\n\n**Use it when** the overview shows errors or latency on a service, or you are changing one service and want to see its effect.\n\n**How to read it**\n- Golden signals (rate, errors, latency): is this service healthy for its callers?\n- Dependencies: is the problem in something it calls? Watch retries and breakers opening (a breaker opens to stop calls to a failing dependency).\n- Kafka consumers: event age over 2 min, growing lag or DLQ publishes mean async work is falling behind or failing.\n- Database & runtime: queueing for a pool connection, slow queries, heap pressure or CPU starvation explain latency that the rows above only show.\n\n**Background:** [Dashboard best practices](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/latest/dashboards/build-dashboards/best-practices/) \u00b7 [Per-service dashboards (Google Cloud)](https://docs.cloud.google.com/stackdriver/docs/solutions/slo-monitoring/ui/svc-dashboard) \u00b7 [Dashboards that matter](https://kindatechnical.com/microservices-architecture/building-observability-dashboards-that-matter.html)",
            "mode": "markdown"
          },
          "repeatDirection": "h",
          "title": "",
          "transparent": false,
          "type": "text"
        }
      ],
      "title": "About this dashboard",
      "type": "row"
    },
    {
      "collapsed": false,
